title: Adopted Sons and Heirs
description: Believers are the sons of God, joint heirs with Christ, sons of the freewoman and not the bondwoman, waiting for the adoption, from the teachings on salvation.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-salvation-adopted-sons.html
highlight: heir

# Built from the teachings under "Adopted sons and heirs" in studies/data/topics/salvation.json,
# with standalone teachings on the same theme. Slide text is the author's own sentences.

=== Sons of God
# from 5281
--- Adopted Sons and Heirs [title]
overline: Doctrine · Salvation
heading: Adopted Sons and Heirs
sub: We who are saved by grace through faith are adopted as sons of God, heirs to His promise and the Kingdom of Heaven.
refs: John 1:12; Romans 8:14-17; Galatians 4:4-7
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 6578
--- Who are the sons of God?
kicker: The doctrine
big: John 1:12
p: Believers. Those that call upon the name of the Lord.
p: Those born again into the promise, adopted sons, heirs to the Kingdom of the Lord.

# from 6578, 12333
--- Joint-heirs with Christ
scripture: Romans 8:14-17 | mark: And if children, then heirs; heirs of God, and joint-heirs with Christ
p: We are heirs of God, joint-heirs with Christ. Not co-religionists with Jews. Not co-heirs with them. But with Christ. And unbelieving Jews have no claim to the promise.

# from 767, 17100
--- Adopted after first believing
lead: In verse 9, he makes it clear that this is a **conditional** state of being. You aren’t adopted without first believing.
big: Romans 8:9
panel-warn: False premises | People get really caught up in free will vs predestination, because they begin with fundamentally false premises, and wrong definitions of terms.
panel: Predestination | The destination of adoption was predetermined for all who enter in through Christ, not predetermining which people would step through the doorway.
refs: Ephesians 1:5; Romans 8:29

# from 13083, 5281
--- Then are the children free
scripture: Matthew 17:25-26 | mark: Then are the children free
p: What a wonderful example of the free gift of salvation, without works. The children are free. They don’t pay tribute to the King.
p: Our entrance to the kingdom is free, for we are at Liberty in Christ. We pay nothing, not our works or labors or deeds. It is a gift of God given to all who believe.
note: But while we sojourn here on earth, we pay tribute to whom tribute is due. Princes of a better country.

=== The freewoman and the bondwoman
# from 4471, 12333
--- Abba, Father
big: Galatians 4:6
p: That we who believe have the Spirit of the Son within us. That we have that quickened spirit, born again crying “Abba!” (Father) to God.
p: The Spirit itself bears witness to this adoption. That we are the children of God, and those without Christ are none of His.

# from 4471, 7133
--- Sons of the freewoman
scripture: Galatians 4:28-31 | mark: we are not children of the bondwoman, but of the free
p: Thus we who are born again in the Spirit become heirs, while those trying to work their way into the kingdom, those under bondage, are denied.

# from 7133
--- Do ye not hear the law?
big: Galatians 4:21
panel-warn: The judaizers | “Yes it’s by faith alone but you have to do the works of the law to be saved. You have to adhere to our vain traditions. To our carnal ordinances. To our dietary restrictions. You don’t expect to just be handed salvation? Do you?”
panel: Sarah | Just as Sarah was barren from birth, and brought to old age, it took a miracle of God, visited upon her, to bring her the promise. Not by anything she did, for she was not capable, but in God all things are possible.
callout: If you’re trusting in your own works, if you’re sewing your own fig leaves, if you’re committing adultery with Hagar to produce your salvation, repent. Hear the law.

=== The adoption
# from 17302, 4471
--- Under tutors and governors
scripture: Galatians 4:1-2
p: The son can be heir but under a schoolmaster, tutors and governors, yet in the fullness of time, be as the Lord, an inheritor of all.
p: The study of the word is like unto princes under tutors, until the day of adoption. The resurrection where we come into our power as glorified sons of God.

# from 17302
--- Waiting for the adoption
lead: We become sons of God when we are born again, but notice the adoption is at the resurrection. At the day of redemption.
big: Romans 8:23
p: The Greek word Paul uses for ‘adoption,’ *huiothesia*, carries a heavier legal meaning than our modern idea of adoption. It was the formal ceremony, the “placing as a son,” where an heir reached the age of maturity, the father publicly recognized them as a legal adult, granting them the full authority, a signet ring, and power to manage the estate.

# from 17302, 17138, 6578
--- We shall be like Him
big: 1 John 3:2
p: At the adoption, when we put on immortality and shed corruption, when we are redeemed, our end will be glorious, as we will be like Him.
p: Even the least in the Kingdom of Heaven is a prince, who will judge with Him in the millennium. We will judge angels.
refs: 1 Corinthians 6:3; Job 42:12

# from 4585
--- All believers are saints
panel-warn: A select few | It is not a select few whose works were so good that they are honored here on Earth with the title. By making a church of man the arbiter, and basing it on works, the Catholic church has cheapened the term.
panel: All who believe | All believers are saints. It’s a title bestowed throughout to all who believe. I am a saint. If you believe you are a saint as well. Even if you’re backslidden.
note: And as saints we should turn from sin, we should live a righteous life as possible. Live up to it. [[Ephesians 1:1]]

# from 6578
--- What manner of love
big: 1 John 3:1
p: Take comfort in this knowledge, joy in the incomprehensible love God has shown us, that we may be adopted joint heirs with His only begotten Son, Christ Jesus.
refs: 2 Corinthians 6:18; Philippians 2:15

